I'll start by exploring the project to understand the existing structure, design system, and any existing mockups or templates I should follow.Let me search for existing mockups, templates, docker/infra related components, and the design system.Let me look for existing mockup files/templates and check the existing analytics/metrics views for design patterns.Let me check the API layer for any existing docker/workspace/infra endpoints to mirror realistic payloads, and look at the workspaces components for data shapes.Now I have a clear picture: codx-junior is a Vue 3 + DaisyUI/Tailwind dark app (`dockview-theme-abyss`) with a workspace model that maps directly to Docker containers (templates, sysbox, traefik labels, lifecycle start/stop/logs). There are **no existing mockups**, so I'll create a self-contained, runnable `infra.html` at the project root, matching the codx-junior dark design system.

---

## 1. Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core requirements**
- A new **Infra view** showing every deployed Docker container ("all docker stuff"): containers, compose stacks, images, volumes, networks, events.
- Must help users **see what's deployed at a glance** (state, health, image, ports, CPU/mem, uptime) and act on it (start/stop/restart, logs, exec, inspect, open).
- Deliver as a **functional HTML mockup** per the Mockups profile: single file, mocked REST API, real interactions, loading/empty/error states, persistence.

**Strategic approach**
- App-shell (static sidebar + topbar) with a dynamic mount, matching codx-junior tokens.
- Realistic `DB` seeded from the codx-junior world (`codxjunior/codx-junior`, `…-default-workspace`, traefik, postgres, redis, ollama, monitoring).
- One `mockFetch` + route table mirroring a plausible `/api/infra/*` REST contract.
- Single `state` + `render()`; mutations via `actions.*`; partial re-renders to keep search focus.
- Cover loading / empty / error + `localStorage` persistence + "Reset mock".

**Dependencies & risks**
- No bundler build. Pinned CDNs (Tailwind 3.4.1 + Font Awesome 6.5.2). Component CSS is plain (not `@apply`) so layout stays coherent if the Tailwind CDN fails.
- No real network calls — everything routes through `mockFetch`.

**Target files**
- `infra.html` (new) — project root, alongside `index.html` / `github_issues.html`.

---

## 2. Mock API Contract (that the UI calls)

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose | Payload shape |
|---|---|---|---|
| GET | `/api/infra/hosts` | Docker hosts/endpoints | `{ hosts:[{id,name,endpoint,engine,os,cpu_cores,cpu_pct,mem_total,mem_used,disk_total,disk_used,is_local}] }` |
| GET | `/api/infra/summary?host=` | Host gauges + counts | `{ host, cpu_pct, mem_*, disk_*, counts:{running,stopped,paused,unhealthy,images,volumes,networks}, engine }` |
| GET | `/api/infra/containers?host=&state=&stack=&q=` | Container list | `{ total, containers:[Container] }` |
| GET | `/api/infra/containers/:id` | Container detail | `Container` |
| GET | `/api/infra/containers/:id/logs?tail=` | Log lines | `{ lines:[{ts,level,msg}] }` |
| GET | `/api/infra/containers/:id/stats` | CPU/mem series | `{ current:{cpu_pct,mem_used,mem_limit,net_rx,net_tx,block_read,block_write,pids}, series:[{t,cpu,mem}] }` |
| POST | `/api/infra/containers/:id/actions` | start/stop/restart/pause/unpause | `{ action }` → `Container` |
| POST | `/api/infra/containers` | Run new container | `{ name,image,ports,env,cmd }` → `Container` |
| DELETE | `/api/infra/containers/:id` | Remove container | `{ ok:true }` |
| GET | `/api/infra/stacks?host=` | Compose projects | `{ stacks:[{name,path,status,services,host_id}] }` |
| GET | `/api/infra/images?host=` | Images | `{ images:[{repo,tag,id,size,created,containers,dangling}] }` |
| GET | `/api/infra/volumes?host=` | Volumes | `{ volumes:[{name,driver,mountpoint,size,in_use,stack,anonymous}] }` |
| GET | `/api/infra/networks?host=` | Networks | `{ networks:[{name,driver,scope,subnet,internal,containers}] }` |
| GET | `/api/infra/events?host=` | Recent docker events | `{ events:[{ts,type,action,actor}] }` |

`Container` = `{ id, short, name, image, image_id, state, health, status_text, created, started_at, uptime_seconds, host_id, stack, service, ports[], cpu_pct, mem_used, mem_limit, net_rx, net_tx, block_read, block_write, restart_count, restart_policy, labels{}, env[], mounts[], networks[], cmd[], entrypoint, healthcheck, url, sysbox }`

Now the mockup file.

