I'll explore the navigation/menu structure so the infra entry lands in the right places.## 1. Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core requirements**
- Make the new `InfraView` reachable from the app's navigation system (not just as an unreferenced file).
- Register it as a first-class **app** so it works on *both* runtimes the codebase uses:
  - **Desktop mode** (`.../desktop`) → opens as a dockview **panel**
  - **Single/mobile mode** → opens as a **route** (`/:projectName/infra`)
- Add a **menu entry** in the main menu.

**Strategic approach**
The project has a clean 4-layer registration chain — I only need to touch each layer once:

| Layer | File | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| 1. App registry | `src/config/apps.js` | Declares the app (`id`, `title`, `component`, `icon`, `route`) |
| 2. Component map | `src/config/appComponentsMap.js` | Binds `component` → Vue component |
| 3. Router | `src/router/index.ts` | Project-scoped URL for single/mobile mode |
| 4. Nav + action | `src/components/main-menu/MainMenuItems.vue`, `src/store/ui.js` | Menu entry + `openInfra()` action |

`openApp()` in `router/navigate.js` already handles the panel-vs-route decision, so no branching is needed anywhere.

**Dependencies & risks**
- ⚠️ **Necessary side fix:** `InfraView.vue`'s root is `p-4 md:p-6 pb-28` with **no height/overflow**. Inside a dockview panel (`h-full`) its content would be clipped with no scrollbar. Adding `w-full h-full overflow-auto` to the root is required for it to actually display. (One-line change, no visual redesign.)
- `src/api/api.js` **already** has `infraModule` imported + `get infra()` exposed — no change needed there.
- Backend note: the `/api/infra/*` routes are contractually **admin-only**. The menu entry is currently *ungated* (mock serves everyone); once the backend enforces the `admin` role, add `v-if="$users.isProjectAdmin"` to the `<MenubarItem>` (same pattern as *Knowledge*).

**Target files**
- `src/config/apps.js` — **modify** (add `infra` app)
- `src/config/appComponentsMap.js` — **modify** (import + map)
- `src/router/index.ts` — **modify** (add route)
- `src/components/main-menu/MainMenuItems.vue` — **modify** (menu entry)
- `src/store/ui.js` — **modify** (add `openInfra()` action)
- `src/views/infra/InfraView.vue` — **modify** (root gets `w-full h-full overflow-auto`)

---

## 2. Minimum Changes Approach

| # | File | Change | Why |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `config/apps.js` | New `infra` entry | Single source of truth for "how to open an app" |
| 2 | `config/appComponentsMap.js` | Map `'infra'` → `InfraView` | Panel + route renderer both resolve components here |
| 3 | `router/index.ts` | `/:projectName/infra` | URL for single/mobile mode + refresh-safe deep link |
| 4 | `store/ui.js` | `openInfra()` action | Menu calls `$ui.openInfra()` (mirrors `openGitView()`) |
