## Design / architecture notes

1. **Three sources of truth, one truth needed.** `MainMenuItems.vue`, `WindowsMenuItems.vue` and `AppsSection.vue` each hard-code their own app list. `APPS` in `config/apps.js` already carries `id / title / icon / route` — the menu lists should be **derived from it** (`Object.values(APPS).filter(a => a.showInMenu)`), otherwise every new view will keep getting "added" to a list nobody renders.
2. **Admin gating is a real risk, not cosmetics.** `/api/infra/*` includes `stop`, `restart` and `remove`. Until the backend enforces `role === 'admin'`, anyone who can see the entry can stop production containers. Gate the `NavItem` (`v-if="$users.isProjectAdmin"`) and set `admin: true` on the `WindowsMenuItems` entry the moment the contract is enforced — this is the highest-severity item here.
3. **Dead code cleanup (optional, not done).** `src/components/MobileMenu.vue` is imported nowhere (mobile uses `DesktopSidebar` with `:is-mobile="true"`). Deleting it removes the fourth stale list.
4. **Touch target check (mobile).** `NavItem` renders ≥44px height per row, so the new sidebar entry is thumb-reachable in the mobile drawer — no extra styling needed. On `InfraView` mobile cards the primary Start/Stop/Resume buttons already use full-width `btn` rows, consistent with your earlier requirement.

