## 4. File Change Summary

| File Path | Action | Component / Section | Change Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `src/views/infra/useInfra.js` | Modify | `openContainer(id, tab)` | Tab is now a parameter (default `'overview'`) instead of being hardcoded — `Logs`/`Stats` can land on the right tab. Logs/stats are fetched only for the requested tab; the rest still load on demand via `setDetailTab()`. |
| `src/views/infra/useInfra.js` | Modify | `askAction`, `askRemove` | Null-guards (`if (!container) return`) plus `name/id` fallbacks, so a click while the drawer detail is still loading opens the confirm dialog instead of throwing. |
| `src/views/infra/ContainersPanel.vue` | Modify | card layout actions | Every action button uses `@click.stop`; **Logs** calls `openContainer(c.id, 'logs')`. The card/identity click still opens the drawer on Overview. |
| `src/views/infra/ContainersPanel.vue` | Modify | table layout actions | Every action button uses `@click.stop` (in addition to the existing `<td @click.stop>` region guard); **Logs** calls `openContainer(c.id, 'logs')`. |

### Behaviour after the change

| User action | Before | After |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Click row / card header | Drawer → Overview | Drawer → Overview (unchanged) |
| Click **Logs** icon | Drawer → **Overview** ❌ | Drawer → **Logs** tab, log lines loading |
| Click **Stop / Restart / Pause / Start** | Confirm dialog, but the click could also bubble to the row and open the drawer | Confirm dialog only — propagation stopped at the button |
| Click **Inspect** | JSON modal (could be paired with an unwanted drawer open) | JSON modal only |
| Click **Remove** (list or drawer) | Confirmation dialog — but silently did nothing when `detail` was still `null` | Always opens the danger confirm dialog ("Remove `<name>`?" / Cancel · Remove) |

### Try it
1. Click a container row → drawer opens on **Overview**.
2. Click the **file-lines** icon in that row → drawer opens directly on **Logs** with lines listed.
3. Click **Stop** → only the confirm dialog appears ("running processes will be terminated"); cancel it and the drawer must not have opened.
4. Click the **trash** icon → confirm dialog appears; **Cancel** keeps the container; **Remove** deletes it and a toast confirms.
5. Resize the panel below 768 px (cards) and above it (table) — both layouts behave the same.

