## 1. Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core Requirements**
1. Clicking the **Logs** action must land on an **active Logs tab** (not fall back to Overview).
2. Container details become a **centered modal** (wide, tall) instead of the right-hand drawer, so logs get real space.

**Why the Logs tab can still end up inactive**

| # | Cause | Fix |
|---|-------|-----|
| 1 | `openContainer()` is `async` and re-assigns `state.detail` **after** the await. Any second invocation (row click race, action from the drawer, polling refresh) resolves later and re-asserts the *default* tab, silently flipping back to Overview. There is no guard against an older `openContainer` finishing last. | Add an `openSeq` token; only the newest open may commit `detail` **and** re-assert the requested tab after the await. |
| 2 | The tab strip is `overflow-x-auto` + `flex-nowrap`. In the narrow drawer the active tab can be scrolled out of view, so an active Logs tab *looks* inactive. | Wide modal + `scrollIntoView` on the active tab whenever the tab changes. |
| 3 | In-flight `loadLogs()` / `loadStats()` responses apply to `state.selectedContainerId` **whenever they resolve** — a stale response for container A can land while B is open. | Guard every async loader against an id mismatch. |

**Target files**
- `src/views/infra/useInfra.js` — `openContainer()` token + tab re-assert; stale-response guards in `loadLogs` / `loadStats` / `refreshSelected`; `doAction` only reloads logs when that tab is visible.
- `src/views/infra/ContainerDrawer.vue` — centered modal, Esc/focus handling, full-height log pane, follow-tail, tail size, sticky tab strip that reveals the active tab.

`InfraView.vue` and `ContainersPanel.vue` need no change — the Logs buttons already call `openContainer(c.id, 'logs')`.

## 2. Minimum Changes Approach
`useInfra.js` first (state machine correctness), then the modal component. Nothing else is touched.

